Key Responsibilities&#xa0;
 Take technical ownership of internal engineering tools and their existing codebases. Develop enhancements, resolve defects, maintain documentation, manage releases, and provide ongoing support to the engineering team.&#xa0;

 Develop and validate AI-assisted workflows that translate product requirements into specifications for each engineering discipline. Work with domain experts to preserve traceability to source requirements and manage dependencies and requirement changes.&#xa0;

 Build automated tests and review workflows to assess the completeness, consistency, and correctness of generated specifications. Ensure outputs can be checked and approved by the responsible engineers.&#xa0;

 Translate user feedback into tool improvements, maintain integrations with engineering workflows, and evaluate additional AI/LLM applications for requirements analysis, documentation, RTL development, and verification.&#xa0;

 Translate system and product requirements into digital specifications and micro-architectures. Develop RTL in Verilog/SystemVerilog and integrate embedded processors, memories, peripherals, register maps, and on-chip buses into mixed-signal SoCs.&#xa0;

 Own digital design activities including lint, CDC/RDC analysis, synthesis, static timing analysis, and low-power design. Support physical implementation and timing closure.&#xa0;

 Collaborate with system, analog, verification, firmware, and physical design teams on SoC integration, clock and reset architectures, mixed-signal interfaces, design reviews, and verification planning.&#xa0;

 Support silicon bring-up, laboratory debugging, and product validation through the transition to volume production Proven hands-on experience developing and integrating AI-based tools into IC design workflows is required. Candidates must be able to demonstrate implemented solutions in areas such as requirements engineering, specification generation, RTL design, verification, or design-flow automation.&#xa0;

 MSc or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Microelectronics, Computer Engineering, or a related field.&#xa0;

 Typically 5+ years of relevant experience in digital IC/SoC design, with experience taking designs from specification through successful silicon.&#xa0;

 Strong practical experience with Verilog/SystemVerilog, RTL design, and digital subsystem integration.&#xa0;

 Solid understanding of SoC architectures, including embedded processors, memories, peripherals, register architectures, and on-chip buses such as AMBA AHB/APB.&#xa0;

